Subject: [PATCH] Bounded single-thread selector bridge for the isolated
 whole-restore harness

Replace the thread-per-connection relay (recv 256 KiB + sendall, 900 s select) at both bridge
ends with one selectors loop per end: recv_into a fixed scratch buffer, one pooled 64 KiB chunk per
direction (genuine backpressure), half-close forwarding, per-end and per-endpoint caps that refuse
the newcomer (never evict an existing flow), connect/status/idle/half-closed-idle/stalled-send
deadlines (stall only while bytes wait), bounded kernel socket buffers, clean stop, and bridge stats
in result.json (success requires both loops ended). Status byte and probe semantics unchanged.
whole_restore start gains validated --bridge KEY=INT. Adds real-socket bridge tests, capacity
pressure tests, mutation controls and loopback load tools.
